<title>USA: AMD settles dispute with SEC.</title>
<headline>AMD settles dispute with SEC.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advanced Micro Devices Inc said it settled a dispute with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission about the company's public disclosures on the development of Am486 microprocessors in 1992 and 1993.</p>
<p>Advanced Micro said it agreed to a cease and desist order from committing future violations of SEC rules and regulations governing official company reports and disclosure of material information.</p>
<p>No fines were imposed and only the company was named as the subject of the order.</p>
</text>
